  "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=5({4}^{x})-3?$",
  "worked_solution": "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y=5({4}^{x}).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938518/assets/add3fbcce9c5e213fa21f8cb4744384653ef182d9cf8a94d32c05c7c5a05812e.png)\n\n- Then, vertically shift it by $3$ units down to give $y=5({4}^{x})-3.$ The point $(0,5)$ moves to $(0,2)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=-3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13938518/assets/8134008472093442320629049fafa0646e0705c32a406abbf50bd90c27110ebe.png)",
